\import [[$:/plugins/mblackman/slipstream/widgets/ui-primitives]]
Slipstream includes a toolkit of lightweight, responsive UI primitives built with modern TiddlyWiki v5.4.0+ custom widgets (`\widget`). They adapt automatically to mobile, tablet, and desktop screens without requiring custom CSS.

---

! 1. Hero Banner (`<$ss.hero>`)

Renders a prominent header banner for dashboards, hubs, or project spaces.

| !Attribute | !Type | !Default | !Description |
| `title` | string | `""` | Primary heading text |
| `subtitle` | string | `""` | Secondary descriptive text |

!! Live Example

<$ss.hero title="Knowledge Base" subtitle="A structured index demonstrating wide-mode breakout and responsive cards."/>

!! Wikitext Syntax

```wikitext
<$ss.hero
  title="Knowledge Base"
  subtitle="A structured index demonstrating wide-mode breakout and responsive cards."
/>
```

---

! 2. Responsive Grid (`<$ss.grid>`)

Creates a CSS Grid container that automatically wraps child elements based on available container width (`repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min, 1fr))`).

| !Attribute | !Type | !Default | !Description |
| `min` | string | `240px` | Minimum width per column before wrapping |
| `gap` | string | `16px` | Gap spacing between grid cells |

!! Live Example

<$ss.grid min="200px">
  <$ss.card badge="Alpha" accent="#3b82f6">
    <h4>Column 1</h4>
    <p>Auto-fits to container width.</p>
  </$ss.card>
  <$ss.card badge="Beta" accent="#10b981">
    <h4>Column 2</h4>
    <p>Maintains consistent gap spacing.</p>
  </$ss.card>
  <$ss.card badge="Gamma" accent="#f59e0b">
    <h4>Column 3</h4>
    <p>Wraps cleanly on mobile.</p>
  </$ss.card>
</$ss.grid>

!! Wikitext Syntax

```wikitext
<$ss.grid min="200px">
  <$ss.card badge="Alpha" accent="#3b82f6">
    <h4>Column 1</h4>
    <p>Auto-fits to container width.</p>
  </$ss.card>
  ...
</$ss.grid>
```

---

! 3. Content Card (`<$ss.card>`)

An elevated container card with rounded corners, subtle border, optional accent edge, and hover states.

| !Attribute | !Type | !Default | !Description |
| `badge` | string | `""` | Text shown in upper-right pill badge |
| `accent` | string | `""` | CSS color for accent border (e.g. `var(--tpc-primary)`) |

!! Live Example

<$ss.card badge="Featured" accent="var(--tpc-primary)">
  <h3>Interactive Content Card</h3>
  <p>Cards accept any valid wikitext, including links, lists, or custom widgets.</p>
  <$ss.progress value="85" total="100" label="Resource Health"/>
</$ss.card>

---

! 4. Property Pill (`<$ss.prop-pill>`)

A two-segment key/value chip. Used automatically by Slipstream beneath tiddler titles (`field` mode), or inline anywhere in your notes (`name`/`value` mode).

| !Attribute | !Type | !Default | !Description |
| `name` / `label` | string | `field` | Display label for the property key |
| `value` | string | `""` | Static property value text (when omitted, reads `field` from current tiddler) |
| `field` | string | `"status"` | Tiddler field name to display or edit |
| `values` | string | `""` | Space-separated options to render an interactive `<select>` dropdown |

!! Live Example

<$ss.prop-pill name="Status" value="Active"/>
<$ss.prop-pill name="Priority" value="High"/>
<$ss.prop-pill name="Version" value="0.1.0"/>

!! Wikitext Syntax

```wikitext
<!-- Static key/value pills -->
<$ss.prop-pill name="Status" value="Active"/>
<$ss.prop-pill name="Priority" value="High"/>

<!-- Dynamic tiddler field pill with interactive select options -->
<$ss.prop-pill field="status" label="Status" values="Draft Active Archived"/>
```

---

! 5. Progress Bar (`<$ss.progress>`)

A smooth progress bar with automatic percentage calculation and optional label.

| !Attribute | !Type | !Default | !Description |
| `value` / `done` | number | `"0"` | Current numeric progress |
| `total` | number | `"100"` | Maximum numeric progress |
| `label` | string | `"Progress"` | Label displayed above progress bar |

!! Live Example

<$ss.progress value="7" total="10" label="Project Milestones"/>

<div style="height: 10px;"></div>

<$ss.progress value="92" total="100" label="Overall Completion"/>

!! Wikitext Syntax

```wikitext
<$ss.progress value="7" total="10" label="Project Milestones"/>
<$ss.progress value="92" total="100" label="Overall Completion"/>
```
